اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

2
00:00:24,529 --> 00:00:31,064
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

3
00:00:34,356 --> 00:00:42,956
The Muslims assembled their army of 40 to 45,000 soldiers

4
00:00:44,214 --> 00:00:49,268
while, their opponent was about 250,000.

5
00:00:51,300 --> 00:01:03,110
And Heraclius has chosen the battlefield, by sending a letter to his brother Theodore, who was the head of his armies.

6
00:01:03,701 --> 00:01:16,062
He said: Choose a place that offers a lot of space for fighting, but very narrow for retreat.

7
00:01:16,547 --> 00:01:19,162
Because he wanted to force his soldiers into fighting,

8
00:01:19,202 --> 00:01:25,323
they've already experienced fighting the Muslims, in a few incidents before.

9
00:01:25,363 --> 00:01:29,474
You have the Battle of Mu'ta(مؤته) and then Ajnadeen(أجنادين) that just happened before Al-Yarmook(يرموك).

10
00:01:30,123 --> 00:01:31,711
The one, we talked about last time.

11
00:01:31,911 --> 00:01:35,410
In which Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) went to rescue Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) in Falastine(فلسطين)

12
00:01:36,179 --> 00:01:42,602
and they routed the Roman army and it was disastrous defeat for the Roman emperor.

13
00:01:42,930 --> 00:01:47,792
So now he assembled a huge army and he told his brother, Theodore,

14
00:01:48,379 --> 00:01:51,625
 to make sure that there's no place to retreat.

15
00:01:52,315 --> 00:01:54,859
So we can force our soldiers to fight.

16
00:01:55,486 --> 00:02:02,569
So in addition to them, having their backs towards the cliff, overlooking the valley of Al-Yarmook(أليرموك),

17
00:02:03,224 --> 00:02:10,394
