44
00:04:28,313 --> 00:04:32,520
In the front Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) placed a very small group of cavalry

45
00:04:33,234 --> 00:04:40,039
that could be very fast in maneuvering and would not be very restricted in their movement.

46
00:04:40,064 --> 00:04:43,296
He placed them in the front and then in the rear,

47
00:04:43,489 --> 00:04:48,335
he placed 5000 soldiers under the leadership of Saeed Bin Zaid(سعيد بن زيد).

48
00:04:48,833 --> 00:04:55,202
And the role of this group of 5000 was to defend

49
00:04:55,227 --> 00:05:00,508
and take care of the Muslim families and their property.

50
00:05:01,473 --> 00:05:05,205
See with all of these Mujahideen(مجاهدين) they came in with their families

51
00:05:05,230 --> 00:05:07,888
and their wealth, their property, everything, Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

52
00:05:09,010 --> 00:05:11,773
And you can't just leave them somewhere without protection.

53
00:05:12,507 --> 00:05:17,050
So they had to accompany the army in order to be close to the protection.

54
00:05:17,875 --> 00:05:21,841
So it was a very risky business don't think that for the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم

55
00:05:21,881 --> 00:05:24,272
and the ones, who joined them, it was an easy thing.

56
00:05:24,319 --> 00:05:31,419
 I mean, you just enlist in the army and go and fight for six months and then you're back, it was such a sacrifice.

57
00:05:31,668 --> 00:05:34,459
Now not all of them would take their families with them,

58
00:05:34,484 --> 00:05:38,118
but the ones who came from very distance and faraway lands,

59
00:05:38,475 --> 00:05:41,176
they will bring in their families and they will just settle in that land.

60
00:05:41,788 --> 00:05:45,092
And many of these fighters when Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) was opened,

61
