00:28:56,252 --> 00:28:58,873
and Allah Alam(ألله أعلم) how Khalid Ibn Walid رضي الله عنه made that judgment.?

377
00:28:58,898 --> 00:29:03,472
Maybe it's by the response that he's seeing from them or the looks on their faces.

378
00:29:03,843 --> 00:29:07,951
He said: Just attack them and surround them.

379
00:29:07,976 --> 00:29:14,558
So they rounded the army from three sides and their back was towards the trench.

380
00:29:15,209 --> 00:29:19,181
Now obviously, there's such a huge army to besiege.

381
00:29:19,643 --> 00:29:21,437
So what Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) then did,

382
00:29:21,744 --> 00:29:29,406
He commanded his men to drive a wedge between the cavalry and the infantry, of the Roman army.

383
00:29:30,149 --> 00:29:31,647
So they succeeded in doing that.

384
00:29:31,787 --> 00:29:34,987
So now the cavalry is separated from the infantry.

385
00:29:35,360 --> 00:29:38,413
The horsemen are separate from the foot soldiers.

386
00:29:39,299 --> 00:29:42,305
And then Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) gave his command to Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص),

387
00:29:42,386 --> 00:29:47,345
he told him open an exit door for the cavalry.

388
00:29:47,800 --> 00:29:51,755
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) knew that their will, to fight is over,

389
00:29:52,185 --> 00:29:54,044
and now they just want to survive.

390
00:29:54,458 --> 00:29:58,236
He knew that they have been pushed to the limit, and that's the end of the resistance.

391
00:29:58,392 --> 00:30:01,874
So he told Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) to open up because now they're surrounded from each side.

392
00:30:02,160 --> 00:30:04,200
He told him: Open up, give them a way out,

393
00:30:04,461 --> 00:30:07,576
and as soon as Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) did that, the cavalry just ran out.

394
00:30:08,250 --> 00:30:13,843
And they went into the desert, each one is trying to survive.

395
00:30:15,032 --> 00:30:17,311
So now you have the foot soldiers without any cover.

396
00:30:18,538 --> 00:30:24,464
And that is when the Muslim army just started pushing them further and further and further.

397
00:30:25,815 --> 00:30:37,254
Now At-Tabari(ألطبري) says that as soon as two men out of the 10 were knocked away, were killed and knocked off the cliff.

398
00:30:37,555 --> 00:30:39,617
 They would drag the entire group.

399
00:30:41,308 --> 00:30:47,589
He said that 80,000 Roman soldiers plunged into the cliff, 80,000.

400
00:30:49,450 --> 00:30:56,733
The total number of losses among the Roman army totaled around 120,000 Soldiers.

401
00:30:57,716 --> 00:31:02,877
80,000 of them in the cliff, they were just falling in numbers, because by now it was nighttime.

402
00:31:03,747 --> 00:31:07,364
And the soldiers are just running away and they don't know what which direction to take.

403
00:31:07,797 --> 00:31:09,721
So some of them are just jumping off the cliff.

404
00:31:10,065 --> 00:31:14,881
Plus, these men, who were chained up their chains ended up killing them.

405
00:31:15,721 --> 00:31:17,828
And that was the prophecy of Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص), he said;

406
00:31:17,852 --> 00:31:19,132
وقلما ياتي بمحصور بخير

407
00:31:19,156 --> 00:31:22,866
These people have cornered themselves, a cliff and chains, that's all what you need.

408
00:31:25,114 --> 00:31:30,370
And Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) spent his night in the pavilion of Theodore.

409
00:31:30,434 --> 00:31:31,678
Theodore himself was killed.

410
00:31:31,916 --> 00:31:39,373
So now Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) is staying in the tents of the Roman General and the fight is going on at night.

411
00:31:39,398 --> 00:31:45,209
They're just finishing off these soldiers, the ones who are left behind and couldn't run away.

412
00:31:46,111 --> 00:31:51,400
So it was a great victory for the Muslim and that's why

413
00:31:51,544 --> 00:31:56,817
the day of Al-Yarmook(يرموك) is such a memorable event in the history of Islam.

414
00:31:58,029 --> 00:32:01,179
Not only because of what happened during the day of Al-Yarmook(يرموك),

415
00:32:01,203 --> 00:32:06,958
but because Al-Yarmook(يرموك) was actually the turning point in the Fatoohaat(فتوحات) of Ash-Sham(ألشَّام)

416
00:32:07,233 --> 00:32:10,661
because of what happened during Al-Yarmook(يرموك)

417
00:32:11,884 --> 00:32:16,224
the resistance of the Roman Empire in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) was broken.

418
00:32:16,673 --> 00:32:22,067
And after that, it was just one city falling after another.

419
00:32:24,324 --> 00:32:28,929
And Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) was the gateway to Africa and to Europe.

420
00:32:29,816 --> 00:32:33,573
That is how the Muslims opened Egypt and then North Africa.

421
00:32:35,502 --> 00:32:37,582
So it was a very, very important event.

422
00:32:39,198 --> 00:32:43,455
3000 Muslims died, among them were many Sahabah(صحابه),

423
00:32:44,530 --> 00:32:46,558
one of them was Ikrimah Bin Abi Jahal(عكرمة بن أبي جهل).

424
00:32:49,108 --> 00:32:51,194
And the situation of Ikrimah(عكرمة) is fascinating

425
00:32:51,219 --> 00:32:53,997
because Ikrimah(عكرمة) first of all, he's the son of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل)

426
00:32:55,173 --> 00:33:00,623
the worst enemy of Rasool Allah ﷺ, the Firaun(فرعون) of this Ummah(امة), he is pharaoh of this Ummah(امة).

427
00:33:01,306 --> 00:33:06,912
Number two Ikrimah(عكرمة) himself was not different than his father.

428
00:33:08,527 --> 00:33:13,581
Ikrimah(عكرمة) was the second most important figure

429
00:33:13,636 --> 00:33:16,254
after Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

430
00:33:17,354 --> 00:33:19,811
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) at that time was fighting against the Muslims.

431
00:33:20,120 --> 00:33:21,611
It was Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) and Ikrimah(عكرمة),

432
00:33:21,971 --> 00:33:26,877
who routed the Muslims and caused the defeat of the Muslims in the battle of Uhud(أحَد).

433
00:33:27,526 --> 00:33:31,165
Ikrimah Bin Abi Jahal(عكرمة بن أبي جهل) was one of the worst enemies of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

434
00:33:31,551 --> 00:33:32,647
until Fath-E-Makkah(فتح مكه).

435
00:33:34,177 --> 00:33:36,790
On the day of Yarmook(يرموك), look at what Ikrimah(عكرمة) did?

436
00:33:37,926 --> 00:33:43,244
Ikrimah(عكرمة) said: I have fought against Rasool Allah ﷺ, so many times,

437
00:33:45,367 --> 00:33:48,086
now on this day shall I retreat.

438
00:33:49,374 --> 00:33:54,439
I have fought against Muhammadﷺ so many times I need to make up for that.

439
00:33:55,611 --> 00:33:59,430
So on this day when Allah is giving me a chance, shall I retreat.

440
00:34:00,970 --> 00:34:04,068
So to ensure that he's going to fight until the last moment,

441
00:34:04,590 --> 00:34:10,077
he called upon his close associates and he was ahead of a squadron.

442
00:34:10,807 --> 00:34:14,813
 He called upon his close associates, among them, his uncle Al-Haris Bin Hishaam(ألحارث بن هشام),

443
00:34:15,090 --> 00:34:16,412
 and Ziraar Ibn Azwar(ضرار إبن أزور),

444
00:34:16,725 --> 00:34:18,983
and many of the others Sahabah(صحابه) and he said:

445
00:34:19,008 --> 00:34:23,521
Let's give each other a pledge to die Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

446
00:34:24,532 --> 00:34:30,061
In other words, we're gonna throw ourselves plunge into the army of the enemy.

447
00:34:32,360 --> 00:34:37,602
And since we made an oath not to live, we need to stay there until we get Shahadah(شَهَادَة)

448
00:34:38,441 --> 00:34:41,327
that's pretty much the Baiyah(بَيْعة) that they gave.

449
00:34:41,535 --> 00:34:43,741
ألبيعة ألموت، تبابعنا على الموت

450
00:34:43,765 --> 00:34:47,412
We pledge allegiance to die, we're not going to come back alive.

451
00:34:48,857 --> 00:34:54,909
And this is by the way, one of the evidences, scholars use for the validity of martyrdom operations

452
00:34:55,044 --> 00:34:56,150
Amaliyatil Istashhadiyyah(عملية الأستشهادية).

453
00:34:56,701 --> 00:34:59,047
That these Sahabah(صحابه) but not all of them are Sahabah(صحابه) obviously.

454
00:34:59,072 --> 00:35:02,359
Ikrimah(عكرمة) was a Sahabi(صحابي), Al-Haris Bin Hishaam(ألحارث بن هشام) was a Sahabi(صحابي),

455
00:35:02,469 --> 00:35:07,019
Ziraar Ibn Azwar(ضرار إبن أزور) was Sahabi(صحابي), the total number of the group was 400, by the way,

456
00:35:07,075 --> 00:35:10,234
 this was not a small group 400, they pledged to die.

457
00:35:10,259 --> 00:35:15,490
Why is it used by the scholars as an evidence to support Al-Amaliyatil Istash'hadiyyah(عملية الأستشهادية),

458
00:35:15,530 --> 00:35:18,337
 it is because of the fact that they promised to die

459
00:35:21,470 --> 00:35:24,048
and to do their best to get Shahadah(شَهَادَة).

460
00:35:26,361 --> 00:35:35,164
The entire group 400, we're laying down on the battleground, so they fulfilled their oath.

461
00:35:36,074 --> 00:35:41,818
Some of them were actually killed and the others were injured so severely that they couldn't move any further.

462
00:35:42,023 --> 00:35:44,513
So they have fulfilled the oath, they did their best.

463
00:35:44,608 --> 00:35:47,813
So the ones, who survived didn't survive because they broke the oath.

464
00:35:47,959 --> 00:35:54,400
They survived because their injuries were so bad, it incapacitated, they couldn't move anymore.

465
00:35:56,120 --> 00:36:02,404
Now, you must have heard about the story of the Sahabah(صحابه), who were dying and then they offered them water.

466
00:36:02,911 --> 00:36:07,684
So each one of them would turn down the offer and say give it to the one next to me.

467
00:36:07,709 --> 00:36:08,856
You heard that story, right?

468
00:36:09,245 --> 00:36:12,610
That actually happened within this group, in Battle of Al-Yarmook(يرموك).

469
00:36:13,564 --> 00:36:18,954
They gave one of them water. So he said: Give it to my brother, he needs it more than I do.

470
00:36:20,148 --> 00:36:22,874
So the water would go to that person, he would say give it to my other brother

471
00:36:22,898 --> 00:36:24,060
who needs this more than I do.

472
00:36:24,822 --> 00:36:28,047
So the water would make a full circle and come back to the same person,

473
00:36:28,072 --> 00:36:31,716
whom it was offered to before, but by the time most of them are already dead.

474
00:36:33,112 --> 00:36:39,142
So this is an example of no fear, willingness to die for the sake of Allah and Eesaar(إيثار)

475
00:36:39,736 --> 00:36:43,677
sacrifice for your brother, he needs the water more than I do.

476
00:36:44,822 --> 00:36:51,083
It was a great victory for the Muslims, but the tone of celebration was subdued.

477
00:36:52,540 --> 00:36:56,239
Because the news of the death of the Khalifah(خليفه) was announced.

478
00:36:58,103 --> 00:37:02,079
According to the story of At-Tabari(ألطبري) before the battle started,

479
00:37:02,900 --> 00:37:07,096
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) receives a messenger from Madina.

480
00:37:09,002 --> 00:37:11,556
The messenger gives Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) a letter

481
00:37:13,166 --> 00:37:17,227
stating that Al-Khalifah(ألخليفه) Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) has passed away

482
00:37:18,004 --> 00:37:19,899
and the new Khalifah(خليفه) is Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

483
00:37:21,097 --> 00:37:28,565
And that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is giving Abu Obaidah Amr Bin Jarrah(أبوعبيدةعمروبن جرَّاح) the command of the Muslim army.

484
00:37:29,371 --> 00:37:33,266
So Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was moved from his post

485
00:37:33,909 --> 00:37:37,326
and was replaced by Abu Obaidah Amr Bin Jarrah(أبوعبيدةعمروبن جرَّاح).

486
00:37:38,830 --> 00:37:42,435
According to At-Tabari(ألطبري) Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) concealed this letter,

487
00:37:43,260 --> 00:37:48,196
and told the messenger not to speak to anyone, and he actually held him,

488
00:37:48,328 --> 00:37:52,287
with him in his tent, to make sure that he's not going to leak out the news.

489
00:37:52,790 --> 00:37:56,877
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) made the judgment that if the news of the death of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق)

490
00:37:56,946 --> 00:38:00,957
reaches to the soldiers in this critical moment, it's not the good timing.

491
00:38:01,673 --> 00:38:05,406
Now, they need to be thinking about what's facing them.

492
00:38:05,843 --> 00:38:12,365
The battle did not start yet, so I don't want to distract them with such catastrophic news

493
00:38:13,406 --> 00:38:15,914
the death of the Khalifah(خليفه) Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

494
00:38:17,688 --> 00:38:22,494
So he decided to hide the news, until the battle was over, and the victory was achieved.

495
00:38:22,923 --> 00:38:26,376
And then he announced the news to the Muslims, and he stepped down

496
00:38:26,736 --> 00:38:30,741
and he handed leadership of the armies in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) to Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة).

497
00:38:31,323 --> 00:38:36,581
And that was basically the last time Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) assumes a position of leadership.

498
00:38:37,244 --> 00:38:41,871
Because Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه has made the decision that

499
00:38:42,067 --> 00:38:45,300
Khalid Ibn Walid رضي الله عنه, his sword is too sharp

500
00:38:46,991 --> 00:38:49,279
and it's time to change him with someone else.

501
00:38:49,671 --> 00:38:52,319
Now Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) as I mentioned to you before, he said that,

502
00:38:52,983 --> 00:38:59,136
The reasoning is that and the wisdom behind that, is that if the Khalifah(خليفه) is very strict,

503
00:38:59,923 --> 00:39:03,568
he has to have somebody under him, who's soft,

504
00:39:04,361 --> 00:39:09,441
and if the Khalifah(خليفه) is soft, then he has to have somebody under him who's very strict.

505
00:39:09,750 --> 00:39:15,341
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق), and Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) go together very well.

506
00:39:16,007 --> 00:39:18,548
One is lenient, and the other one is strict,

507
00:39:18,924 --> 00:39:22,466
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة) go together very well

508
00:39:22,727 --> 00:39:26,698
because Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is very strict and Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة) is very soft and compassionate.

509
00:39:27,836 --> 00:39:32,536
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه he bathed in a day that was very cold,

510
00:39:32,766 --> 00:39:34,553
so he catched a fever.

511
00:39:35,474 --> 00:39:40,261
And his fever was developing day by day so in this situation was getting worse, every day.

512
00:39:41,170 --> 00:39:46,503
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه felt that this is the end of his life.

513
00:39:47,456 --> 00:39:49,061
His life is coming to a closing.

514
00:39:50,652 --> 00:39:58,132
So now the concern of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is who to appoint as my successor.

515
00:39:59,366 --> 00:40:03,524
So he's making Shura(شورى), he invites Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف),

516
00:40:04,733 --> 00:40:09,055
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf رضي الله عنه comes in, Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) asks him,

517
00:40:10,254 --> 00:40:11,742
What do you say about Umar(عُمَر)?

518
00:40:12,925 --> 00:40:14,621
What's your view about Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)?

519
00:40:14,942 --> 00:40:22,086
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) said: Anything that you asked me, you have better knowledge of.

520
00:40:24,211 --> 00:40:28,217
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) is saying that you are the most knowledgeable among us, about everything.

521
00:40:29,897 --> 00:40:32,475
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: I want to hear your opinion.

522
00:40:33,814 --> 00:40:35,805
Abdur Rahman  Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) said;

523
00:40:37,034 --> 00:40:41,694
My view is that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is better than what you think.

524
00:40:43,318 --> 00:40:46,366
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) knew why, Abu Bakr(أبوبكر) was asking him this question.

525
00:40:47,356 --> 00:40:49,474
He knew that he's asking him to determine,

526
00:40:49,950 --> 00:40:52,673
who was the best fit person for the position of Khilafah(خِلَافَه).

527
00:40:53,685 --> 00:40:55,976
So Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) is saying

528
00:40:56,593 --> 00:40:59,920
that he is even better than what do you think.

529
00:41:00,586 --> 00:41:02,988
In other words, he's right person.

530
00:41:04,635 --> 00:41:08,375
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف), by the way, could be one of the contenders for the position.

531
00:41:09,502 --> 00:41:11,270
He is one of the Ashra Mubashireen Bil Jannah(عَشرةمبشرين بالجنَّة).

532
00:41:11,295 --> 00:41:17,247
Now obviously, the post of the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) is not going to go to anyone outside of the 10

533
00:41:17,684 --> 00:41:19,633
 if there's someone among the 10, who's living.

534
00:41:20,437 --> 00:41:25,809
These 10 according to the consensus of the Sahabah(صحابه) are the greatest and these 10 are

535
00:41:25,834 --> 00:41:30,077
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), Umar(عُمَر), Uthman(عثمان), Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب),

536
00:41:30,500 --> 00:41:33,847
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف), Talha Bin Obaidellah(طلحةبن عبيدالله),

537
00:41:34,133 --> 00:41:38,051
Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبير بن عوام), Abu Obaidah Amr Bin Jarrah(أبوعبيدةعمروبن جرَّاح),

538
00:41:38,633 --> 00:41:43,942
Saeed Bin Zaid Bin Nufail(سعيدبن زيد بن نفيل) and Sa'ad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدإبن أبي وقاص),

539
00:41:44,165 --> 00:41:45,051
these are the 10.

540
00:41:45,631 --> 00:41:47,622
So, Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) is one of them.

541
00:41:48,664 --> 00:41:50,824
So he's saying that he is better than what you think.

542
00:41:52,141 --> 00:41:54,034
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said;

543
00:41:54,852 --> 00:41:59,139
Then conceal this matter, and don't tell anyone about it, this conversation.

544
00:41:59,297 --> 00:42:01,775
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) said: Of course! And then he left.

545
00:42:02,242 --> 00:42:05,412
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه invited Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان),

546
00:42:07,452 --> 00:42:10,951
so Uthman(عثمان) came, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said;

547
00:42:12,196 --> 00:42:16,455
What is your view on Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.?

548
00:42:17,439 --> 00:42:21,595
Uthman Ibn Affan رضي الله عنه said: In the Name of Allah,

549
00:42:22,497 --> 00:42:26,590
I believe that what Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) does in private

550
00:42:27,574 --> 00:42:30,003
is better than what he does openly.

551
00:42:31,387 --> 00:42:33,418
Meaning what we see of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

552
00:42:33,484 --> 00:42:35,131
and the greatness of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب),

553
00:42:35,236 --> 00:42:40,372
 the outside of him, what he does in private, when nobody can see him is even better.

554
00:42:40,991 --> 00:42:42,090
 And then he said;

555
00:42:42,291 --> 00:42:44,151
وليس فينا مِثلَ

556
00:42:44,471 --> 00:42:46,753
And there is none among us like him.

557
00:42:47,893 --> 00:42:51,431
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه told Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان), he told him:

558
00:42:52,415 --> 00:42:59,755
If I would bypass, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) it's not going to get beyond you.

559
00:43:01,551 --> 00:43:04,438
If I decide not to appoint Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب),

560
00:43:04,567 --> 00:43:07,363
you are going to be the person in that post.

561
00:43:09,278 --> 00:43:15,908
 And then he invited Usaid Bin Khuzair(أسيدبن خضير) and he sought his opinion on that.

562
00:43:16,470 --> 00:43:18,181
And Usaid Bin Khuzair(أسيدبن خضير) said;

563
00:43:18,206 --> 00:43:20,834
اللهمَّ أعْلم ألخير بعدك

564
00:43:21,444 --> 00:43:24,137
I think that he's the best after you.

565
00:43:24,971 --> 00:43:29,376
He is happy with what makes the Muslims pleased.

566
00:43:29,412 --> 00:43:34,407
He is pleased with what pleases the Muslims, and he dislikes what the Muslims dislike,

567
00:43:34,432 --> 00:43:38,305
meaning he is the man for the Ummah(امة), he cares for the Ummah(امة).

568
00:43:38,967 --> 00:43:43,610
His concern is for the Ummah(امة), if something pleases the Ummah(امة), it pleases him.

569
00:43:44,173 --> 00:43:47,414
If something harms the Ummah(امة), he dislikes that.

570
00:43:48,368 --> 00:43:52,586
He is not a person, who will look for his own benefit to the detriment of the Ummah(امة).

571
00:43:53,099 --> 00:43:54,915
He is a person, who will live for us.

572
00:43:57,076 --> 00:44:02,383
Everyone Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه consults would give him the same answer,

573
00:44:02,579 --> 00:44:05,907
similar answers, with the exception of Talha Bin Obaidellah(طلحةبن عبيدالله),

574
00:44:06,165 --> 00:44:08,075
he is the only one who had a different view.

575
00:44:09,204 --> 00:44:11,605
He told Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, he said;

576
00:44:12,259 --> 00:44:18,595
What will your answer be to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ on the Day of Judgment when He asks you

577
00:44:20,165 --> 00:44:25,910
about appointing Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه to lead us, when you know his harshness.

578
00:44:27,597 --> 00:44:31,191
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه that was his makeup that was his personality

579
00:44:31,731 --> 00:44:34,494
he's a very strong man.

580
00:44:35,329 --> 00:44:41,668
And he had this great presence and he demands respect and his physical stature was huge.

581
00:44:42,884 --> 00:44:44,561
So that added to his presence.

582
00:44:45,683 --> 00:44:51,455
Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري) he once went knocking on the door of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه,

583
00:44:51,924 --> 00:44:55,104
he knocks three times and Umar(عُمَر) did not answer back.

584
00:44:55,432 --> 00:44:56,457
So Abu Musa(أبوموسى) left.

585
00:44:56,730 --> 00:44:58,934
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he came out and said: Why did you leave?

586
00:44:59,825 --> 00:45:02,278
Abu Musa(أبوموسى) said: Because I heard Rasool Allah ﷺ say that

587
00:45:02,303 --> 00:45:06,268
if you ask for permission three times and you're not given it, then leave.

588
00:45:06,585 --> 00:45:09,553
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: You're gonna bring me another witness,

589
00:45:09,772 --> 00:45:11,041
that Rasool Allah ﷺ said that.

590
00:45:12,022 --> 00:45:14,835
Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري) left and he went to a meeting of Al-Ansaar(اَلْاَنْصَار),

591
00:45:15,325 --> 00:45:17,957
Abu Saeed Al-Khudri(أبوسعيدألخدري) who is narrating this story. He says:

592
00:45:17,989 --> 00:45:23,144
When Abu Musa(أبوموسى) came in his face was yellow, the color of his face changed.

593
00:45:24,196 --> 00:45:25,464
They said: What happened to you?

594
00:45:25,753 --> 00:45:28,281
He said: Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said that I have to bring a witness

595
00:45:28,534 --> 00:45:30,011
that Rasool Allah ﷺ said this.

596
00:45:30,456 --> 00:45:35,922
Abu Saeed Al-Khudri(أبوسعيدألخدري) said: The youngest among us, will go with you as a witness.

597
00:45:36,682 --> 00:45:41,460
The Ansaar(ألأنْصَار) their youngsters would study with Rasool Allah ﷺ, Hadith(حديث),

598
00:45:42,446 --> 00:45:44,778
while some of the other Sahabah(صحابه) were busy with work.

599
00:45:45,657 --> 00:45:49,223
They had stores they had farms, they had jobs

600
00:45:49,247 --> 00:45:52,536
so they couldn't spend all of their time with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

601
00:45:53,556 --> 00:45:57,344
But the youth because their families are taking care of them.

602
00:45:57,985 --> 00:46:01,147
They could afford spending all of their time with Rasool Allah ﷺ,

603
00:46:01,592 --> 00:46:04,682
or some of the other Sahabah(صحابه) who made the conscious decision to do so,

604
00:46:04,888 --> 00:46:08,514
like Abu Hurairah رضي الله عنه, he paid the price for that. He said:

605
00:46:08,539 --> 00:46:11,551
وكُنْتُ ألْزَمُ رَسولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عليه وسلَّمَ علَى مِلْءِ بَطْنِي،

606
00:46:11,985 --> 00:46:15,331
He said: I would accompany Rasool Allah ﷺ on an empty stomach

607
00:46:15,433 --> 00:46:20,411
because when Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) in the later days would narrate all of these Ahadith(احاديث).

608
00:46:20,587 --> 00:46:24,050
Some people started questioning Abu Hurairah(أبوهريرة)

609
00:46:24,097 --> 00:46:26,237
 and saying how come you know all of these Ahadith(احاديث)

610
00:46:26,270 --> 00:46:30,577
while the Sahabah(صحابه), who became Muslim before you don't know all of this Ahadith(أحاديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

611
00:46:31,066 --> 00:46:34,948
Abu Hurairah(أبوهريرة) said: Because they had work to do, they had businesses, they had farms,

612
00:46:35,161 --> 00:46:38,784
but I had nothing and I would accompany Rasool Allah ﷺ on an empty stomach

613
00:46:40,106 --> 00:46:44,132
so one of the young Sahabah(صحابه) went and was witness for Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري),

614
00:46:44,179 --> 00:46:46,693
but the point to make is that that was the personality of Umar(عُمَر).

615
00:46:48,235 --> 00:46:54,134
So Talha(طلحة) said that what will your response be to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ on the Day of Judgment.

616
00:46:56,198 --> 00:46:58,058
Now Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said:

617
00:46:58,078 --> 00:46:58,992
أجلِسُونِي

618
00:46:59,870 --> 00:47:04,854
Because he was laying down, so he wanted them to make him sit, straight.

619
00:47:06,276 --> 00:47:08,776
He said: Are you threatening me by Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.?

620
00:47:10,633 --> 00:47:13,609
If Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ asks me: Why did I appoint Umar(عُمَر)?

621
00:47:13,808 --> 00:47:15,998
I will say because he's the best among us.

622
00:47:17,462 --> 00:47:22,019
Every person in his personality, there are things that you might dislike,

623
00:47:22,371 --> 00:47:23,597
but Umar(عُمَر) is the best among you.

624
00:47:25,980 --> 00:47:29,812
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was, he took this comment seriously

625
00:47:31,183 --> 00:47:32,972
because he reminded him by Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

626
00:47:33,012 --> 00:47:35,019
So Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: This is, what I'll say.

627
00:47:35,396 --> 00:47:36,916
And another narration,

628
00:47:37,853 --> 00:47:40,275
 "أمَّرتُ عليهم ألقويُّ الأمين"

629
00:47:40,443 --> 00:47:43,617
If Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ asks me: Why do you appoint Umar(عُمَر) I will say

630
00:47:43,874 --> 00:47:47,854
because he is Al-Qawwi(ألقوي), Al-Ameen(ألأمين) he is strong and the trustworthy.

631
00:47:48,241 --> 00:47:55,903
And these were the two words that the daughter of the man in Mad'yan(مدين) used when she went to her father.

632
00:47:56,228 --> 00:48:01,524
 After Musa عليه السّلام provided their flock with water.

633
00:48:01,759 --> 00:48:05,839
She went back to her father and said: O my father, why don't you hire that man?

634
00:48:06,397 --> 00:48:09,876
Because the best man to hire is a man, who's strong and trustworthy

635
00:48:10,436 --> 00:48:15,848
and that's how Musa(موسى) got a job in Mad'yan(مدين) and he lived there for 10 years.

636
00:48:17,124 --> 00:48:20,379
So this woman or girl at the time, she was very young.

637
00:48:20,570 --> 00:48:22,569
She was very wise in that statements.

638
00:48:22,593 --> 00:48:24,491
So, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ mentions it in Qur'an

639
00:48:24,764 --> 00:48:27,120
that these are the two requirements if you want to hire someone.

640
00:48:28,133 --> 00:48:32,180
This is what you look for, in an interview when you want to hire somebody to work for you.

641
00:48:32,899 --> 00:48:36,248
 Is he strong? And strength here doesn't mean necessarily physical strength.

642
00:48:36,280 --> 00:48:40,206
It means competency in that particular field.

643
00:48:40,611 --> 00:48:42,044
So you're strong in the field.

644
00:48:42,523 --> 00:48:44,597
You're competent in that particular field.

645
00:48:44,993 --> 00:48:48,848
If it's a physically demanding work, then the person has to be physically fit.

646
00:48:49,232 --> 00:48:53,820
If it's a mentally demanding work, then the person needs to be mentally fit and strong.

647
00:48:54,380 --> 00:48:57,548
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was the perfect person for this role.

648
00:48:58,131 --> 00:49:03,018
He was very intelligent, very wise, very strong, very determined.

649
00:49:03,857 --> 00:49:07,045
He had solid opinions, he can make decisions

650
00:49:07,563 --> 00:49:10,129
and he demanded respect from the people around him.

651
00:49:10,563 --> 00:49:13,566
And that's why Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: I'm going to appoint him to lead you.

652
00:49:14,430 --> 00:49:18,838
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه called Abu Obaidah رضي الله عنه to write down

653
00:49:20,346 --> 00:49:23,349
the appointment of Umar(عُمَر), so it was written down.

654
00:49:24,237 --> 00:49:27,363
And then he had it announced in the Masjid(مسجد)

655
00:49:27,765 --> 00:49:30,507
and then he had the people give Baiyah(بَيْعة) to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

656
00:49:30,532 --> 00:49:31,730
while he was still alive.

657
00:49:31,992 --> 00:49:36,229
So the Baiyah(بَيْعة) of Umar(عمر) did not happen, after the death of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

658
00:49:36,633 --> 00:49:39,132
As soon as Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه died

659
00:49:39,221 --> 00:49:42,439
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) immediately assumed his position as Khalifah(خليفه)

660
00:49:43,182 --> 00:49:46,406
there was no Baiyah(بَيْعة) that happened after the death, it was already done

661
00:49:46,768 --> 00:49:51,811
and completed before the death of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

662
00:49:53,049 --> 00:50:01,228
The illness of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) carried on, and his situation was getting worse,

663
00:50:02,040 --> 00:50:04,276
until it was the 15th day.

664
00:50:05,567 --> 00:50:10,226
So Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) asked his daughter Ayesha(عائشه), he said: What day did Rasool Allah ﷺ die?

665
00:50:11,801 --> 00:50:16,561
She said: He died on a Monday, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: And this is Monday.

666
00:50:18,028 --> 00:50:20,505
So I think that this will be my last day.

667
00:50:23,180 --> 00:50:25,726
Now this is a very interesting statement.

668
00:50:26,824 --> 00:50:30,907
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was very keen on following Rasool Allah ﷺ

669
00:50:31,346 --> 00:50:35,135
his whole Khilafah(خِلَافَه) is an example of followings Sunnah(سنة).

670
00:50:37,029 --> 00:50:39,771
And not just following Sunnah(سنة) in things that don't cost you anything.

671
00:50:41,029 --> 00:50:46,356
He was following Sunnah(سنة) on issues that could cost him and the entire community, their life.

672
00:50:46,568 --> 00:50:51,539
The issue of sending out the army of Osama(أسامة) was not something to be taken light.

673
00:50:51,564 --> 00:50:53,730
That was a very serious risk,

674
00:50:54,429 --> 00:50:57,624
and then insisting on having Osama(أسامة) lead the army and

675
00:50:57,649 --> 00:51:00,582
not appointing somebody older than him. He was only 18 years old.

676
00:51:01,046 --> 00:51:03,651
And then the fact that he never changed the post of

677
00:51:03,747 --> 00:51:07,380
anyone appointed by Rasool Allah ﷺ and make it clear,

678
00:51:07,405 --> 00:51:10,089
إِنَّمَا أَنَا مُتَّبِعٌ وَلَسْتُ بِمُبْتَدِعٍ

679
00:51:10,452 --> 00:51:14,026
That I am a man, who will follow and I'm not a man who will innovate.

680
00:51:14,687 --> 00:51:17,511
I'm going to follow Rasool Allah ﷺ and I'm not going to come up with Bid'ah(بدعة).

681
00:51:18,562 --> 00:51:26,208
He was very insistent, and persistent on following the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ to the letter.

682
00:51:27,787 --> 00:51:31,893
And it seems that he even wanted to follow the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ in his death,

683
00:51:32,296 --> 00:51:35,915
so he expected that he would die on the same day as Rasool Allah ﷺ died.

684
00:51:37,022 --> 00:51:42,521
And it happened, he died on a Monday and Rasool Allah ﷺ died on a Monday

685
00:51:42,788 --> 00:51:47,459
and Rasool Allah ﷺ died at the age of 63 and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) dies at the age of 63.

686
00:51:47,733 --> 00:51:51,589
So he's following Rasool Allah ﷺ, in his life and in his death.

687
00:51:54,118 --> 00:51:55,943
His last words, in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) were,

688
00:51:56,924 --> 00:51:59,646
تَوَفَّنِي مُسْلِمًا وَأَلْحِقْنِي بِالصَّالِحِينَ

689
00:52:00,377 --> 00:52:05,277
My Lord, take me as a Muslim and join me with the righteous,

690
00:52:06,080 --> 00:52:12,382
take me as a Muslim and make me join the righteous, make me join my closest friend Muhammadﷺ,

691
00:52:12,635 --> 00:52:15,987
and make me join the Sahabah رضي الله عنه who passed away before.

692
00:52:16,197 --> 00:52:18,588
These were his last words, in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

693
00:52:20,541 --> 00:52:25,997
He died the 21st of Jama Al-Aakhirah(جمادالآخِرة) the 13th year of Hijrah(هجرة).

694
00:52:26,735 --> 00:52:30,986
So, his Khilafah(خِلَافَه) was two years, three months and 10 days that was it.

695
00:52:31,912 --> 00:52:36,575
All of these events, battles, Da'wah(دعوة)

696
00:52:38,419 --> 00:52:41,176
were done within two years, three months and 10 days.

697
00:52:42,211 --> 00:52:52,056
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه had the honor of leading the Salah(صلاة) of Janazah(جنازة) on Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

698
00:52:52,438 --> 00:52:57,262
Now when I think about this, the Imam(اِمَام) of Salat-Ul-Janazah(صلاة الجنازة) makes Dua(دُعَا) for the person, who dies.

699
00:52:57,929 --> 00:53:02,968
The Imam(اِمَام) makes a Dua(دُعَا) and everybody behind the Imam(اِمَام) is also making Dua(دُعَا) for the deceased.

700
00:53:04,213 --> 00:53:10,669
So you can imagine Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه covered in the Thaub(ثوب), the cloth, the white cloth,

701
00:53:11,542 --> 00:53:14,229
 and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is the one leading the Salah(صلاة) on him

702
00:53:14,320 --> 00:53:17,959
and he is one making Dua(دُعَا) for Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, it's Umar(عُمَر)

703
00:53:18,372 --> 00:53:23,355
making Dua(دُعَا) for his close friend Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

704
00:53:24,122 --> 00:53:26,884
asking Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ to grant him the highest level in Jannah(جنة).

705
00:53:28,658 --> 00:53:32,590
And then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and Uthman Ibn Affan رضي الله عنه

706
00:53:33,197 --> 00:53:36,818
and Talha Bin Obaidellah(طلحة بن عبيدالله) and Abdur Rahman Ibn Abi Bakr(عبدالرحمن إبن أبي بكر)

707
00:53:37,723 --> 00:53:43,842
were the ones, who would lower the body of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه in his grave.

708
00:53:44,809 --> 00:53:50,935
The grave of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه would be in the room of his daughter Ayesha(عائشه)

709
00:53:52,828 --> 00:53:55,748
right next to the grave of Muhammadﷺ.

710
00:53:56,815 --> 00:54:03,562
And out of respect for Muhammadﷺ, the head of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

711
00:54:05,262 --> 00:54:09,935
was placed at the same level as the shoulders of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

712
00:54:10,911 --> 00:54:16,008
So he's not put right next to him, but he's a little bit behind.

713
00:54:16,522 --> 00:54:21,140
 Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر) he says I came rushing I wanted to enter into the grave and lower the body.

714
00:54:21,609 --> 00:54:25,612
But I came after the body was already lowered and my father told me it's already done.

715
00:54:26,186 --> 00:54:29,087
But the ones, who did that were Umar(عُمَر), Uthman(عثمان), Talha(طلحة)

716
00:54:29,141 --> 00:54:32,271
and Abdur Rahman Ibn Abi Bakr رضي الله عنهم أجمعين

717
00:54:34,033 --> 00:54:41,512
After two years, three months and 10 days Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه succeeded in.

718
00:54:42,363 --> 00:54:46,849
Number one, establishing the rules of Khilafah(خِلَافَه) in Islam.

719
00:54:48,040 --> 00:54:55,481
Number two, starting the mission of carrying out the Da'wah(دعوة) to the entire world

720
00:54:56,767 --> 00:55:02,888
because during the time of Muhammadﷺ, the Da'wah(دعوة) was still within the peninsula.

721
00:55:04,933 --> 00:55:08,360
And the only exception to that was Mu'tah(مَؤتَة) and Tabook(تبوك).

722
00:55:10,037 --> 00:55:14,545
But even with Mu'tah(مَؤتَة) and Tabook(تبوك), even though they were within Roman territory,

723
00:55:15,092 --> 00:55:20,267
but it was still populated by Arab tribes in these southern parts of Ash-Sham(ألشَّام),

724
00:55:21,408 --> 00:55:24,910
but it was Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, who started the mission of Da'wah(دعوة),

725
00:55:26,525 --> 00:55:32,251
into the different nations of the world, the Persian people, the Roman people and beyond.

726
00:55:33,190 --> 00:55:42,081
So he was the teacher and the guide of the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) and the Duaah(دعاة) both.

727
00:55:43,268 --> 00:55:49,323
He never had allowed himself the luxury of having spare time.

728
00:55:50,843 --> 00:55:54,312
He never allowed himself the luxury of relaxing

729
00:55:55,145 --> 00:56:00,595
and he never allowed himself to benefit financially from his post.

730
00:56:01,009 --> 00:56:06,816
We did talk earlier about the demands of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) in his salary and even the bargaining.

731
00:56:07,644 --> 00:56:09,403
When he said that this is not enough.

732
00:56:10,736 --> 00:56:18,771
 But he was doing it because he had a certain standard of living that he has to take care of himself and his family.

733
00:56:18,841 --> 00:56:21,000
In addition to that he was very generous.

734
00:56:22,224 --> 00:56:30,018
Before he died, since he still had some wealth leftover from his business days,

735
00:56:30,276 --> 00:56:33,241
before Khilafah(خِلَافَه) he had pieces of land.

736
00:56:35,401 --> 00:56:38,901
He told his daughter Ayesha(عائشه), I want you to sell my property

737
00:56:39,225 --> 00:56:41,920
and then to pay back to the Muslim treasury.

738
00:56:42,718 --> 00:56:45,468
All of the money that I took as a salary when I was Khalifah(خليفه).

739
00:56:47,171 --> 00:56:50,696
I have the money, give it back to the Muslim Treasury.

740
00:56:51,464 --> 00:56:53,663
When Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) heard about that, he said;

741
00:56:54,150 --> 00:56:56,502
رحم الله أبا بكر، لقد أتعب من بعده

742
00:56:57,283 --> 00:56:58,619
May Allah have mercy on Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

743
00:56:59,001 --> 00:57:01,076
he's making a difficult on the ones, who will come after him.

744
00:57:02,408 --> 00:57:06,311
He's setting a standard that is too high, he's going to make it difficult on us.

745
00:57:07,584 --> 00:57:10,053
 You return all of the money that you have taken from the treasury

746
00:57:10,078 --> 00:57:11,557
even though it was Halal(حلال) for you.

747
00:57:12,545 --> 00:57:16,388
You deserve, it was not a deserve, it was less than what he deserves.

748
00:57:18,813 --> 00:57:21,393
He got the money because he had to support a family.

749
00:57:21,469 --> 00:57:25,364
And now since he has money left over, he's gonna pay it back to the Treasury.

750
00:57:26,360 --> 00:57:30,869
So all of what was taken by Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was returned to Bait-Al-Maal-Al-Muslimeen(بيت المال المسلمين).

751
00:57:33,777 --> 00:57:40,345
صَّلَواةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِ ألأولين والآخرين محمد إبن عبدالله وَعلى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

752
00:57:40,537 --> 00:57:46,556
سبحانك اللهم وبحمدك نشهد و الله إله إلَّا أنت نستغفرك ونتوب عليك

